WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:03.302
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.772
-This is it.
What a -- what a year.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.641
2020. It's been
one of my favorites.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.210
Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.545
There's --

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.048
I can tell you one thing
that is cancelled for sure --

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.650
Coughing in public.
That's over.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.253
You just -- you go
into a restaurant

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.055
and just drink water wrong,

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.924
you just got to get up and go
to your car and drive home.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.593
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.029
The whole restaurant just
stares at you.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.498
It's going to be hardest on my
parents, because my parents,

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.900
there's nothing more that they
love than coughing in public.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.737
It's one of their favorite
things to do.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.039
I mean, I haven't had
a conversation with my dad

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.775
in ten years without him choking
the whole time.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:47.179
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.115
And you have to go -- anytime
you go to a restaurant too now,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.449
they take your temperature.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.686
It's just a teenager that
doesn't know what he's doing.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.789
Doesn't even hold it up
near my head.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.891
He's just like, "45 degrees,
you're good."

00:00:58.891 --> 00:00:59.993
You're like, "Am I?"

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:03.763
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.965
He's not even fazed by it.
He's like --

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.500
I'm like,
"Dude, I think I'm dead.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.303
That's not -- I should go
to the hospital."

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.072
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.642
Everybody acts like they've
already had COVID, too.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.310
Everybody's like,
"I think I had it in February."

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.779
You're like, "Did you?"
They're like...

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:22.381
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:23.883
"I think so."

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.352
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.689
I remember I sneezed a lot
one week, and then...

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.825
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.027
There's --

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.963
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:40.800
My wife and I, we have a --
we have an 8-year-old daughter,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.903
and so we're having to do
the virtual learning.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.204
And they're like, "Just do --

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.539
you know, just teach her
school stuff."

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.974
You're like, "It's good.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.943
I barely made it out of high
school, let me give it a go."

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.944
Uh...

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:55.047
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.283
And she's doing -- she's
doing Common Core math.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.751
She brought home new math.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.986
That's what they want us to --

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.055
I don't even know
what this math is.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.522
And they're like,
"Here's the new one."

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.125
You're like, "Oh, great,
I get to watch a 40-minute

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.860
YouTube video
on Common Core math."

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.963
And it's not like the old math
was doing bad.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.565
It's doing great.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.067
It's not like we're getting
incorrect change everywhere

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:18.504
and we're just sitting there
like, "This stupid old math.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.306
I wish new math
would come along."

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.643
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.414
If you don't --
I don't know if --

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.015
if you don't know
Common Core math,

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:35.788
it's just basically a long way
to get to the same answer.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.991
It's like -- it's like, how can
we use the entire sheet of paper

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:43.395
for this math problem?

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:46.933
And even when you break it down,
you see old math sneak in there.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.002
I mean, you're --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.503
You're like, that was old math
right there.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.104
Just do that at the beginning

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:53.939
and we won't even
have to be in this.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:59.579
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.680
There is --

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.283
[ Applause ]

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:07.920
I told my wife, "It's a long way
to get to the same thing."

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.723
It would be -- if you came
to my house,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.258
and you knocked on the
front door and you're like,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.726
"Can I come in?"
and I was like,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.862
"Could you walk around and come
in through the back door?"

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:19.065
And you would be like, "Does
the front door not work?"

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.301
Like, "It works.
It works fine.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.703
I use it. Most people
still use it.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.540
But the new way is to go
jump the fence,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.110
come in back,
and then meet me back here."

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.380
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.451
One thing
my daughter does miss

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:42.689
is she was starting to ride
the bus, which was very fun.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.023
And when she first started
riding the bus,

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:47.126
we switched schools,
and it was in first grade.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.562
First day of school,
we walked her to the bus stop.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.497
It was a very, very fun day.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.399
And then at the end
of the school day,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.935
someone from the school
called my cell phone.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:59.005
They have my wife's cell phone
and they have my cell phone.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.806
So they called my cell phone
and they said,

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.375
"Hey, do you know
what bus number

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.309
your daughter is
supposed to be on?"

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:06.279
I said, "I'm her dad."

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:10.916
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.485
I was like,
"This is how you thought --

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.754
You saw a mom and dad's
cell phone and said,

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.756
'I bet the dad knows'?"

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.758
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.926
"I mean, do you have parents?

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:22.494
Were you raised with a family?

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:25.498
Have you ever seen families
out before?

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.999
You thought,
'Let's call the husband,

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.702
I bet he knows.'?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.905
Unless there's two husbands,
you should never call a husband

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.340
a day in your life.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.175
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:39.245
I -- I would rather you ask
a lady

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.780
that doesn't know her
walking by.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.448
I think he could get to
the bottom of it

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.350
quicker than I can."

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.852
And finally, I just said,
"All right, I'll get her.

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:49.321
What's the name of the school?"
Uh...

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:52.958
All right, that's it for me.
Thank you guys very much.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.093
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.093 --> 00:04:56.528
-Nate Bargatze.

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:58.331
For tour dates and ticket info,

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.700
go to nategargatze.com.

